# Real captured LTE RRC PDU -- SystemInformationBlockType1 (BCCH-DL-SCH-Message)
# 18 bytes / 144 bits, carried on SI-RNTI (RNTI 0xffff in the srsRAN MAC context).
#
# SOURCE   : https://github.com/SysSec-KAIST/LTESniffer  (licence: AGPL-3.0)
# FILE     : pcap_file_example/ltesniffer_dl_mode.pcap
# COMMIT   : a694803082017ac2b349e6b113940e8b9ba2fe5b
# URL      : https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SysSec-KAIST/LTESniffer/a694803082017ac2b349e6b113940e8b9ba2fe5b/pcap_file_example/ltesniffer_dl_mode.pcap
# PCAPSHA  : be4972206afe95e8cc2a76f1312a648a7011795d5112782b4986317986fc0340
# FRAME    : 1 (identical PDU in 1432 of the 2433 frames; 1790 frames are SI-RNTI)
# CARRIER  : pcap link type 147 (DLT_USER0) holding srsRAN "mac-lte-framed"
#            context (radioType, direction, rntiType, tag/value pairs; tag 0x01
#            introduces the payload -- srsRAN lib/src/common/pcap.c, which is
#            the layout Wireshark's packet-mac-lte.c expects for DLT_USER0).
# CAPTURED : over the air by LTESniffer (SDR sniffer) from an srsRAN srseNB
#            testbed, 2023-04-25 13:17 CEST. The LTESniffer README states:
#            "Some examples of pcap files that contain decoded traffic between
#            srseNB and a test smartphone". Real radio, real hardware, but a
#            LAB eNB, not a commercial network -- MCC 901 is the ITU test MCC.
# CELL     : trackingAreaCode 0007 (7), cellIdentity 0019b01 (105217),
#            freqBandIndicator 7, systemInfoValueTag 0, scheduling rf16
#            sibType3 (Wireshark dissection of the same pcap).
# LICENCE  : upstream pcap NOT vendored (AGPL-3.0, and this repository declares
#            no licence of its own); factual 18-byte extract only, re-derivable
#            with ./tools/check-lte-corpus.sh <workdir> --upstream
406404ab00070019b0181460108280000000
